---
/**
 * Every markdown table in a guide, wrapped in its own scroll container.
 *
 * Registered as the lowercase `table` entry in the `components` map that
 * [slug].astro hands to <Content />, so it applies to tables written in
 * markdown pipe syntax without touching a single content file.
 *
 * Why a wrapper element and not `display: block; overflow-x: auto` on the
 * <table> itself: changing a table's display value drops its table role in
 * assistive technology, and a comparison table with no row/column semantics is
 * worse than one that scrolls badly.
 *
 * tabindex="0" makes the region reachable from the keyboard. A scrollable box
 * that only a mouse or a finger can move fails WCAG 2.1 SC 2.1.1, and that is
 * exactly what an overflow container without it is.
 *
 * The scroll affordance (a shadow on whichever edge still has table behind it)
 * is `.guide-table` in src/styles/globals.css.
 */
---

<div class="guide-table" tabindex="0">
  <table>
    <slot />
  </table>
</div>
